    {
      "id": "arch-local",
      "from": 0,
      "duration": 14,
      "text": "Behind the room: Vite, strict TypeScript, and a hand-built SVG interface. One state store connects scheduling, outfits and packing. Your day stays in localStorage; music uploads use IndexedDB. Intelligence is optional. The core works locally."
    },
    {
      "id": "arch-routing",
      "from": 14,
      "duration": 15,
      "text": "Live requests use your browser key directly, or a Vercel proxy with a server secret. Spark understands intent and photos. Captain tries Wonder, then Spark, then a labeled local fallback. Baseten is a separate, optional provider."
    },
    {
      "id": "arch-routes",
      "from": 29,
      "duration": 14,
      "text": "Each API route has a job. Interpret and propose structure your input. Tag-photo drafts clothing. The Captain routes propose plans. Transcribe handles speech. Dream creates posters; SAM segments images through the proxy. Responses are normalized before use."
    },
    {
      "id": "arch-trust",
      "from": 43,
      "duration": 12,
      "text": "Finally, the trust boundary. Code checks every proposal: fields, IDs, times and conflicts. Fixed events stay fixed. Outfits use available clothes. You review and confirm. One undoable update changes your room. You stay in control."
    }
  ]
}